From: PortareOS <hello@portare.org>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: il97680a: the panel's own vertical timing for every mode

Every mode carried 27 lines of vertical back porch, three more than the
panel's own timing (Android's, for both of its rates: 12 lines of front
porch, 2 of sync, 24 of back porch), so that 1302 x 1001 would make the
119.88Hz mode exactly 120000/1001. The panel holds lock to that only
while variable refresh stretches a frame by about 0.3ms; past it, it
refreshes from its own memory and the frame arriving later tears. On
998 lines it follows the stretch: at 50fps under variable refresh, a
bar sweeping the screen tore on 1001 lines and not on 998, in a blind
comparison and again on its own (#623).

Every mode goes to 998 lines, its pixel clock recomputed for the rate
its comment names; all are within 3.2ppm of it.
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-ilitek-il97680a.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-ilitek-il97680a.c
@@ -154,24 +154,25 @@
 		 * the content, and black frame insertion turns that correction
 		 * into a visible flash.
 		 *
-		 * The rate is exact rather than near. refresh is
-		 * clock * 1000 / (htotal * vtotal), so if htotal * vtotal is a
-		 * multiple of 1001 then 120 * htotal * vtotal / 1001 is a whole
-		 * number of kHz and the division comes back to 120000/1001 with
-		 * nothing left over. 1001 is 7 x 11 x 13; htotal 1302 already
-		 * carries the 7, and vtotal 1001 supplies the rest, which costs
-		 * three extra lines of vertical back porch.
+		 * Every mode here has the panel's own vertical timing, Android's
+		 * for both its rates: 12 lines of front porch, 2 of sync and 24
+		 * of back porch, 998 lines. vtotal 1001 would make this rate
+		 * exact - 1001 is 7 x 11 x 13 and htotal 1302 carries the 7 -
+		 * and the three lines of back porch that costs were tried. The
+		 * panel then held lock only while variable refresh stretched a
+		 * frame by about 0.3ms: at 50fps a bar sweeping the screen tore
+		 * on 1001 lines and not on 998 (#623).
 		 *
-		 *   156240000 / (1302 * 1001) = 119.88011988...
+		 *   155772000 / (1302 * 998) = 119.88031, +1.6ppm
 		 *
-		 * so the frontend never has a correction to make for 59.94
-		 * content and the BFI cadence holds indefinitely.
+		 * A frame in about 3 hours at 59.94, which the frontend's audio rate
+		 * control absorbs.
 		 *
 		 * drm_mode_vrefresh() still rounds this to 120, so the panel's
 		 * frame-rate register (0x60) is programmed 0x00 exactly as
 		 * before - see il97680a_rpnova_init_sequence().
 		 */
-		.clock = 156240,
+		.clock = 155772,
 		.hdisplay = 1280,
 		.hsync_start = 1280 + 12,
 		.hsync_end = 1280 + 12 + 2,
@@ -179,7 +180,7 @@
 		.vdisplay = 960,
 		.vsync_start = 960 + 12,
 		.vsync_end = 960 + 12 + 2,
-		.vtotal = 960 + 12 + 2 + 27,
+		.vtotal = 960 + 12 + 2 + 24,
 	},
 	{
 		/*
@@ -192,14 +193,14 @@
 		 *                                       every 2.3 seconds
 		 *   119.455046 / 59.7275 = 2.0000   <- this one
 		 *
-		 *   155686000 / (1302 * 1001) = 119.45505...
+		 *   155219000 / (1302 * 998) = 119.45473
 		 *
-		 * +0.4ppm from 2 x 59.7275. Same totals as the modes above,
+		 * -2.2ppm from 2 x 59.7275. Same totals as the modes above,
 		 * the pixel clock alone moves; drm_mode_vrefresh() rounds it to
 		 * 119, which is why the frame-rate register is chosen by class
 		 * (il97680a_rate_class()) rather than by that number.
 		 */
-		.clock = 155686,
+		.clock = 155219,
 		.hdisplay = 1280,
 		.hsync_start = 1280 + 12,
 		.hsync_end = 1280 + 12 + 2,
@@ -207,7 +208,7 @@
 		.vdisplay = 960,
 		.vsync_start = 960 + 12,
 		.vsync_end = 960 + 12 + 2,
-		.vtotal = 960 + 12 + 2 + 27,
+		.vtotal = 960 + 12 + 2 + 24,
 	},
 	{
 		/*
@@ -223,9 +224,9 @@
 		 *                                       every 3.2 seconds
 		 *   120.197628 / 60.0988 = 2.0000   <- this one
 		 *
-		 *   156654000 / (1302 * 1001) = 120.197775, +1.2ppm
+		 *   156184000 / (1302 * 998) = 120.197384, -2.0ppm
 		 *
-		 * The same 1001-line frame as every other mode here, the panel's
+		 * The same 998-line frame as every other mode here, the panel's
 		 * own porches. A wider vertical blanking, vtotal 1116 at 174651kHz
 		 * and exact to 0.00ppm, was tried for black frame insertion's
 		 * flip window, and the panel does not lock to it: it scans from
@@ -235,7 +236,7 @@
 		 * (#623). With these porches it follows the input, the stretched
 		 * front porch of variable refresh included.
 		 */
-		.clock = 156654,
+		.clock = 156184,
 		.hdisplay = 1280,
 		.hsync_start = 1280 + 12,
 		.hsync_end = 1280 + 12 + 2,
@@ -243,7 +244,7 @@
 		.vdisplay = 960,
 		.vsync_start = 960 + 12,
 		.vsync_end = 960 + 12 + 2,
-		.vtotal = 960 + 12 + 2 + 27,
+		.vtotal = 960 + 12 + 2 + 24,
 	},
 	{
 		/*
@@ -257,9 +258,9 @@
 		 *                                       every 4.3 seconds
 		 *   119.652237 / 59.82610 = 2.0000   <- this one
 		 *
-		 *   155943000 / (1302 * 1001) = 119.65224...
+		 *   155476000 / (1302 * 998) = 119.65252
